  "id": "rough-and-tumble-play",
  "term": "rough-and-tumble play",
  "definition": "Rough-and-tumble play is playful fighting between willing participants that stays enjoyable through self-control and mutual give-and-take. In this view, it can support psychosocial development by exercising self-regulation and encouraging empathy, prosocial behavior, and social bonding, though it can also escalate if not well moderated.",
